# Creating this file DISABLES Stow's built-in default ignore list,
# so the GNU Stow 2.4.1 defaults are reproduced verbatim below,
# then extended with project-only files that must never be stowed.

# --- GNU Stow default ignore list (preserved) ---
RCS
.+,v

CVS
\.\#.+
\.cvsignore

\.svn
_darcs
\.git
\.gitignore

.+~
\#.*\#

^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING

# --- Project-only context: dotfiles repo CLAUDE.md must stay local ---
# Needed as project memory when cwd=~/dotfiles, but must NOT be stowed to
# ~/CLAUDE.md (would leak dotfiles/Stow context into every $HOME-rooted session).
^/CLAUDE.md

# --- Backup-only: not deployed by Stow ---
# .codex is mutated at runtime by the Codex CLI (marketplace state written back
# into config.toml), and its hooks.json points at ~/.codex, not at this repo.
# Tracked here as a snapshot; symlinking it would make Codex dirty the repo.
^/\.codex
# macOS finder droppings — the default ignore list above does not cover these.
\.DS_Store
# ~/.claude is owned by the claude-config repo's own Stow run; this leftover
# untracked directory must never be stowed over it.
^/\.claude

# --- Repo-internal working directories: never deployed to ~/ ---
# IDE metadata, Superpowers session state, Playwright MCP output, and repo docs
# exist in both dotfiles and claude-config; stowing them makes the two repos
# conflict over the same home paths.
^/\.idea
^/\.superpowers
^/\.playwright-mcp
^/docs
^/tests

# --- Stray directories from unexpanded home paths: never deployed to ~/ ---
# A tool run with cwd=~/dotfiles that fails to expand "~" (or a JVM whose
# user.home resolves to "?") creates these literally; stowing them copies the
# mistake into the home directory.
^/~$
^/\?$
